%% Corrected flow. Two things the earlier version got wrong:
%%   1. The customer never signs a transaction. Every on-chain write is
%%      onlyOperator and is relayed by the backend on the customer's behalf.
%%   2. Self-destruct is an off-chain database deletion. Nothing is erased
%%      on-chain, because nothing on-chain can be erased.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant V as Verifier Bank
    participant B as Backend API<br/>(Cloud Run)
    participant K as Cloud KMS<br/>(HSM)
    participant DB as Cloud SQL<br/>(encrypted PII)
    participant SC as KYCVault.sol<br/>(Ethereum Sepolia)
    actor P as Partner Bank

    rect rgb(238, 246, 255)
    Note over V, SC: 1 - Verification. The hash goes on-chain; the data never does.
    V->>B: POST /api/kyc/verify { customerId, fullName, govId }
    B->>K: Wrap a fresh 256-bit data key
    K-->>B: Wrapped key
    B->>DB: Store AES-256-GCM ciphertext
    B->>B: payloadHash = SHA-256(plaintext PII)
    B->>SC: verifyKYC(customerId, payloadHash)<br/>signed by the KMS operator key
    SC-->>B: Tx hash + KYCVerified event
    Note right of SC: On-chain now holds:<br/>hash, timestamp, verifier address.<br/>No name. No ID number.
    end

    rect rgb(240, 250, 244)
    Note over C, SC: 2 - Consent. The customer decides; the backend relays.
    C->>B: POST /api/consent/grant { partnerId }
    B->>SC: grantConsent(customerId, keccak256(partnerId))
    SC-->>B: ConsentGranted event
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 237)
    Note over P, SC: 3 - Access. The chain is the gatekeeper, not the database.
    P->>B: GET /api/kyc/access/:customerId
    B->>SC: checkStatus(customerId, partnerHash)
    SC-->>B: (consentGranted, isVerified, payloadHash, verifiedAt)
    alt No consent, or not verified
        B-->>P: 403 - denied, and the attempt is logged
    else Consent present
        B->>K: Unwrap the data key
        B->>DB: Read ciphertext, decrypt
        B->>B: Recompute SHA-256 and compare with the on-chain hash
        alt Hashes differ
            B-->>P: 500 - the record was tampered with off-chain
        else Hashes match
            B-->>P: 200 - PII released
        end
    end
    end

    rect rgb(253, 242, 245)
    Note over C, SC: 4 - Revocation and erasure
    C->>B: POST /api/consent/revoke
    B->>SC: revokeConsent(...)  - flag flipped to false, history retained
    C->>B: DELETE /api/kyc/forget
    B->>DB: Delete ciphertext, consents, OTP challenges
    Note right of SC: The on-chain hash remains, now an orphan.<br/>It proves a verification happened;<br/>it cannot reconstruct what was verified.
    end
